Experiment 43: To Handle JavaScript Alert Pop-ups Using Selenium WebDriver

AIM
To write a Selenium WebDriver program to handle JavaScript alert pop-ups by accepting the alert.

## ALGORITHM
1. Start the program.
2. Launch the Chrome browser using Selenium WebDriver.
3. Open the JavaScript alerts practice webpage.
4. Click the button to display the JavaScript alert.
5. Switch the control to the alert pop-up.
6. Accept the alert by clicking OK.
7. Close the browser.

## CODE

**File name: `JavaScriptAlertTest.java`**

```java
import org.openqa.selenium.By;
import org.openqa.selenium.WebDriver;
import org.openqa.selenium.chrome.ChromeDriver;
import org.openqa.selenium.Alert;
import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.*;

public class JavaScriptAlertTest {

    @Test
    public void handleAlert() {

        WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();

        driver.get("https://the-internet.herokuapp.com/javascript_alerts");

        driver.manage().window().maximize();

        driver.findElement(By.xpath("//button[text()='Click for JS Alert']")).click();

        Alert alert = driver.switchTo().alert();

        String alertText = alert.getText();

        System.out.println("Alert Message: " + alertText);

        alert.accept();

        System.out.println("Alert accepted successfully.");

        assertEquals("I am a JS Alert", alertText);

        driver.quit();
    }
}
```

## INPUT
- Website: https://the-internet.herokuapp.com/javascript_alerts
- Button: Click for JS Alert
- Alert message: I am a JS Alert
- Action: Accept (OK)

## EXPECTED OUTPUT

```text
Alert Message: I am a JS Alert
Alert accepted successfully.
```

## RESULT
Thus, the JavaScript alert pop-up was handled successfully using Selenium WebDriver by switching to the alert and accepting it.
